# Frontend Testing Readiness

- Write components in a testable way.
- Avoid tightly coupled implementations.

## Selectors

- Prefer semantic selectors.
- Use stable IDs where necessary.
- Avoid brittle selectors based on CSS classes only.

## Structure

- Keep logic isolated and predictable.
- Separate business logic from rendering when complexity increases.

## Behavior

When implementing features, consider:
- happy path
- validation path
- loading path
- error path
- edge cases